Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>後(后)谿(溪)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6705086"/>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9493899"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Pain and rigidity of the neck, tinnitus, deafness, sore throat, mania, malaria, acute lumbar sprain, night sweating, febrile diseases, contracture and numbness of the fingers, pain in the shoulder and elbow.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The dorsal branch derived from the ulnar nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the little finger, ulnar to the distal phalanx, 0.1 f-cun proximal-medial to the ulnar corner of the little fingernail, at the intersection of the vertical line of ulnar border of the nail and horizontal line of the base of the little fingernail.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9093316"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Houxi</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004300"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011277"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003625"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Small Intestine 3</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The dorsal digital artery and vein, the dorsal venous network of the hand.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>SI 3</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


