        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 92. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>臑兪(俞)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Swelling of the shoulder, aching and weakness of the shoulder and arm.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior cutaneous nerve of the arm, the axillary nerve; deeper, the suprascapular nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the shoulder girdle, superior to the posterior axillary fold, in the depression inferior to the spine of the scapula.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
