        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 38. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>手三里</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Abdominal pain, diarrhea, toothache, swelling of the cheek, motor impairment of the upper limbs, pain in the shoulder and back.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>See Wenliu (LI 7).</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterolateral aspect of the forearm, on the line connecting LI5 with LI11, 2 B- cun inferior to the cubital crease.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4610474"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shousanli</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795332"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002386"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Large Intestine 10</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the radial recurrent artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LI 10</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


