        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 216. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>水溝(沟)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The buccal branch of the facial nerve, and the branch of the intraorbital nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, at the midpoint of the philtrum midline. Remarks: Alternative location for GV26 at the junction of the upper one third and lower two thirds of the philtrum midline.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely upward OJ-0.5 inch.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Renzhong</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shuigou</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005402"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 26</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 26</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The superior labial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 26</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0831517 -->

