        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 35. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>合谷</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1840369"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Headache, pain in the neck, redness, swelling and pain of the eye, epistaxis, nasal obstruction, rhinorrhea, toothache, deafness, swelling of the face, sore throat, parotitis, trismus, facial paralysis, febrile diseases with anhidrosis, hyperhidrosis, abdominal pain, dysentery, constipation, amenorrhea, delayed labour, infantile convulsion, pain, weakness and motor impairment of the upper limbs.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The superficial ramus of the radial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the dorsum of the hand, radial to the midpoint of the second metacarpal bone.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4610474"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Hegu</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003646"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0794954"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Large Intestine 4</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The venous network of the dorsum of the hand.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LI 4</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0886544 -->

