        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 112. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>大腸兪(俞)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5884126"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Low back pain, borborygmus, abdominal distension, diarrhea, constipation, muscular atrophy, pain, numbness and motor impairment of the lower extremities, sciatica.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior ramus of the third lumbar nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the lumbar region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the fourth lumbar vertebra (L4), 1.5 B- cun lateral to the posterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Dachangshu</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004620"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795312"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005462"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Back-Shu Point of the Large Intestine</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The posterior branch of the fourth lumbar artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 25</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0913913 -->

