Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>大包(包)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3779268"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Pain in the chest and hypochondriac region, asthma, general aching and weakness.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The seventh intercostal nerve and the terminal branch of the long thoracic nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the lateral thoracic region, in the sixth intercostal space, on the midaxillary line. Note: With the subject lying on the side and the arm abducted, SP21 is located at the intersection of the midaxillary line and the sixth intercostal space.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4167850"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Dabao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795307"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795308"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795306"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Spleen 21</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The thoracodorsal artery and vein, the seventh intercostal artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>SP 21</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


