        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 222. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>石門(门)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5019725"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Abdominal pain, diarrhea, edema, hernia, anuria, enuresis, amenorrhea, morbid leukorrhea, uterine bleeding, postpartum hemorrhage.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The anterior cutaneous branch of the eleventh intercostal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the lower abdomen, 2 B-cun inferior to the centre of the umbilicus, on the anterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6789717"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shimen</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007118"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795303"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Conception Vessel 5</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Front-Mu Point of Triple Energizer</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>RN 5</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Ren 5</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>See Zhongji (CV 3).</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>CV 5</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1206796 -->

