        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 78. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>食竇(窦)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Fullness and pain in the chest and hypochondriac region.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The lateral cutaneous branch of the fifth intercostal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the anterior thoracic region, in the fifth intercostal space, 6 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line. Note: SP17, ST18 and KI22 are located along the curve of the fifth intercostal space.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4167850"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shidou</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795299"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0016416"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Spleen 17</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The thoracoepigastric vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>SP 17</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1208891 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1208891">
