D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>胃倉(仓)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Abdominal distension, pain in the epigastric region and back, infantile indigestion.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The lateral cutaneous branches of the posterior ramus of the eleventh thoracic nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the 12th thoracic vertebra (T12), 3 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line. Note: BL50 and BL21 are located at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the 12th thoracic vertebra (T12).</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Weicang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004636"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795312"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008231"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 50</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 50</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 50</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 50</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The posterior branches of the subcostal artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 50</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


