        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 184. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>京門(门)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_8260776"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Abdominal distension, borborygmus, diarrhea, pain in the lumbar and hypochondriac region.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The eleventh intercostal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the lateral abdomen, inferior to the free extremity of the 12th rib. Note: GB 25 can be located while the subject is lying on the side with the shoulder flexed. The free extremity of the 12th rib can be palpated below the inferior border of the costal arch posterior to the posterior axillary line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5283975"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Jingmen</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002225"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004611"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795323"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000916"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Front-Mu Point of the Kidney</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>G 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Gallbladder 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>GB 25</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1904200 -->

