Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>氣(气,気)戶</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Fullness in the chest, asthma, cough, hiccup, chest pain and hypochondriac pain.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The branches of the supraclavicular nerve and the anterior thoracic nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the anterior thoracic region, inferior to the clavicle, 4 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6221269"/>
