        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 51. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>缺盆</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Cough, asthma, sore throat, pain in the supraclavicular fossa.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>Superficially, the intermediate supraclavicular nerve; deeper, the supraclavicular portion of brachial plexus.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the anterior region of the neck, in the greater supraclavicular fossa, 4 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line, in the depression superior to the clavicle.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6221269"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Avoid puncturing the artery. Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Quepen</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001105"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795294"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>L 15</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Stomach 15</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>Superiorly, the transverse cervical artery.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>ST 12</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


