                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 42. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>天鼎</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Sudden loss of voice, sore throat, scrofula, goiter.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>Superficially, the supraclavicular nerve. It is on the posterior border of m. sternocleido- mastoideus just where the cutaneous cervical nerve emerges. Deeper, the phrenic nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the anterior aspect of the neck, at the same level as the cricoid cartilage, just posterior to the border of the sternocleido- mastoid muscle. Note: Directly inferior to LI18, at the same level as St10.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4610474"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Tianding</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001128"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002375"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Large Intestine 17</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The external jugular vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LI 17</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2260472 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2260472">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2954517"/>
