                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 204. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>腰兪(俞)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Irregular menstruation, pain and stiffness of the lower back, hemorrhoids, muscular atrophy of the lower extremities, epilepsy.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The branch of the coccygeal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the sacral region, at the sacral hiatus, on the posterior median line. Note: The sacral hiatus is a small depression immediately above the anal cleft.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely upward 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Yaoshu</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0036013"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795312"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005473"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the median sacral artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2678584 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2678584">
