        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 172. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>聽(听,聴)會(会)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Deafness, tinnitus, toothache, motor impairment of the temporomandibular joint, mumps, deviation of the eye and mouth.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The great auricular nerve and facial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, in the depression between the intertragic notch and the condylar process of the mandible. Note: When the mouth is opened, GB2 is located in the depression anterior to the intertragic notch.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5283975"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Tinghui</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004657"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0036212"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>G 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Gallbladder 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The superficial temporal artery.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GB 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2922507 -->

