                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 188. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>膝陽(阳)關(关,関)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Swelling and pain of the knee, contracture of the tendons in popliteal fossa, numbness of the leg.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The terminal branch of the lateral femoral cutaneous nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the lateral aspect of the knee, in the depression between the biceps femoris tendon and the iliotibial band, posterior and proximal to the lateral epicondyle of the femur.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5283975"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Xiyangguan</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000981"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795317"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795324"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001465"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>G 33</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Gallbladder 33</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The superior lateral genicular artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GB 33</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


