                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 96. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>天容</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Deafness, tinnitus, sore throat, swelling of the cheek, foreign body sensation in the throat, goiter.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>Superficially, the anterior branch of the great auricular nerve, the cervical branch of the facial nerve; deeper, the superior cervical ganglion of the sympathetic trunk.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the anterior region of the neck, posterior to the angle of the mandible, in the depression anterior to the sternocleidomastoid muscle. Note: The sternocleidomastoid muscle is more distinct when the head is turned to the opposite side against resistance.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9093316"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Tianrong</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001128"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001684"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000974"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Small Intestine 17</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>Anteriorly, the external jugular vein; deeper, the internal carotid artery and internal jugular vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>SI 17</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3452202 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3452202">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5151019"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/isMemberAcupointOf"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9093316"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5151019"/>
        <dc:description>An acupuncture point that is located along the Small Intestine Meridian of Hand-Taiyang (SI), which consists of 19 standardized acupoints beginning at SI 1 (Shaoze) on the ulnar side of the little finger near the corner of the nail, traveling up the dorsal-ulnar aspect of the arm, across the scapular region, and ascending along the lateral neck and cheek, and ending at SI 19 (Tinggong) in the depression between the tragus and the mandibular condyloid process.</dc:description>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9093316"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Acupoint of the small intestine meridian of hand-taiyang</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Acupuncture point of the small intestine meridian</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Acupuncture point of the small intestine meridian of hand-taiyang</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>SI</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Acupoint of the Small Intestine Meridian</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


