Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>孔最</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4598552"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Cough, pain in the chest, asthma, hemoptysis, sore throat, spasmodic pain of the elbow and arm.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve and the superficial ramus of the radial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the anterolateral aspect of the forearm, on the line connecting LU5 with LU9, 7 B- cun superior to the palmar wrist crease. 
Note: LU6 is 5 B-cun inferior to LU5, 1 B-cun superior to the midpoint of the line connecting LU5 with LU9.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9964503"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Kongzui</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795334"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002386"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>L 6</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Lung 6</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The cephalic vein, the radial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LU 6</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


