Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>急脈(脉)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Lower abdominal pain, hernia, pain in the external genitalia.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The ilioinguinal nerve; deeper, in the inferior aspect, the anterior branch of the obturator nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the groin region, at the same level as the superior border of the pubic symphysis, and 2.5 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5419503"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Jimai</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003699"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008337"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>LIV 12</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>LV 12</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Liver 12</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the external pudendal artery and vein, the pubic branches of the inferior epigastric artery and vein; laterally, the femoral veIn.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LR 12</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


