        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior and medial antebrachial cutaneous nerves; deeper, the posterior and anterior interosseous nerves.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterior aspect of the forearm, just radial to the ulna, 3 B-cun proximal to the dorsal wrist crease. Note: TE7 is ulnar to TE6.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3898257"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
