        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 204. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>長(长)強</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6993030"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Diarrhea, bloody stools, hemorrhoids, prolapse of the rectum, constipation, pain in the lower back, epilepsy.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior ramus of the coccygeal nerve, the hemorrhoid nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the perineal region, inferior to the coccyx, midway between the tip of the coccyx and the anus. Note: The subject may be in prone position or knee-chest position.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.1 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Changqiang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001245"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001350"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002356"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 1</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 1</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the inferior hemorrhoid artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3888808 -->

