        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 27. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>天府</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Asthma, epistaxis, pain in the medial aspect of the upper arm.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The lateral brachial cutaneous nerve at the place where the musculocutaneous nerve passes through.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the anterolateral aspect of the arm, just lateral to the border of the biceps brachii muscle, 3 B-cun inferior to the anterior axillary fold. Note: Longitudinally, LU3 is located at the same level as the junction of the upper one third and lower two thirds of the line con- necting the level with anterior axillary fold to LU5.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9964503"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1 inch.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Tianfu</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001507"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795287"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001460"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>L 3</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Lung 3</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The cephalic vein and muscular branches of the brachial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LU 3</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


