        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 72. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>三陰(阴)交</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Abdominal pain, borborygmus, abdominal distension, diarrhea, dysmenorrhea, irregular menstruation, uterine bleeding, morbid leukorrhea, prolapse of the uterus, infertility, delayed labour, nocturnal emission, impotence, enuresis, dysuria, edema, hernia, pain in the external genitalia, muscular atrophy, motor impairment, paralysis and pain of the lower extremities, headache, dizziness and vertigo, insomnia.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>Superficially, the medial crural cutaneous nerve; deeper, in the posterior aspect, the tibial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the tibial aspect of the leg, posterior to the medial border of the tibia, 3 B-cun superior to the prominence of the medial malleolus. Note: 1 B-cun superior to KI8.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4167850"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable. Acupuncture on this point is contraindicated in pregnant women.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Sanyinjiao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000979"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795305"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003823"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Spleen 6</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The great saphenous vein, the posterior tibial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>SP 6</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4427404 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4427404">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_8364824"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
