                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 214. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>前頂(顶)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Epilepsy, dizziness, blurring of vision, vertical headache, rhinorrhea.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>On the communicating site of the branch of the frontal nerve with the branch of the great occipital nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the head, 3.5 B-cun superior to the anterior hairline, on the anterior median line. Note: GV21 is located at the midpoint of the line connecting GV 20 and GV 22.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Qianding</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795292"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000033"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 21</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 21</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The anastomotic network formed by the right and left superficial temporal arteries and veins.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 21</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


