        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 227. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>中庭</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Distension and fullness in the chest and intercostal region, hiccup, nausea, anorexia.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The medial branch of the anterior cutaneous branch of the sixth intercostal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the anterior thoracic region, at the midpoint of the xiphisternal junction, on the anterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6789717"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Zhongting</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011124"/>
