D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>合陽(阳)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Low back pain, pain and paralysis of the lower extremities.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The medial sural cutaneous nerve; deeper, the tibial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterior aspect of the leg, between the lateral head and medial head of the gastrocnemius muscle, 2 B-cun distal to the popliteal crease. Note: 2 B-cun distal to BL40, on the line connecting BL40 with BL57.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.7- 1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Heyang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001388"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795330"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003823"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 55</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 55</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 55</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 55</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The small saphenous vein; deeper, the popliteal artery and vem.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 55</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


