        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 152. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>天泉</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Cardiac pain, distension of the hypochondriac region, cough, pain in the chest, back and the medial aspect of the arm.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The medial brachial cutaneous nerve and the musculocutaneous nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the anterior aspect of the arm, between the long head and short head of the biceps brachii muscle, 2 B-cun distal to the anterior axillary fold.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4694897"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Tianquan</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001507"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795287"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001460"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>P 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Pericardium 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The muscular branches of the brachial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>PC 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


