        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 59. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>水道(道)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Lower abdominal distension, retention of urine, edema, hernia, dysmenorrhea, sterility.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>A branch of the subcostal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the lower abdomen, 3 B-cun inferior to the centre of the umbilicus, 2 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line. Note: ST28 is 3 B-cun inferior to ST25, 1 B-cun inferior to St27, 2 B-cun lateral to CV4.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6221269"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.7-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shuidao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007118"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795303"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>S 28</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Stomach 28</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the subcostal artery and subcostal vein; laterally, the inferior epigastric artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>ST 28</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5019725 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5019725">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
