        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 129. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>崑(昆)崙(侖,仑)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7315457"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Headache, blurring of vision, neck rigidity, epistaxis, pain in the shoulder, back and arm, swelling and pain of the heel, difficult labour, epilepsy.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The sural nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterolateral aspect of the ankle, in the depression between the prominence of the lateral malleolus and the calcaneal tendon.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Kunlun</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003701"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012291"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004454"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 60</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 60</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 60</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 60</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The small saphenous vein, the posteroexternal malleolar artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 60</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


