        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 145. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>腹通(通)谷</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Abdominal pain and distension, vomiting, indigestion.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the upper abdomen, 5 B-cun superior to the centre of the umbilicus, 0.5 B-cun lateral to the anterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4813389"/>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Futonggu</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007118"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795301"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>K 20</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Kidney 20</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>See Shlguan (KI 18).</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>KI 20</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


