        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 47. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>巨髎(髎)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Facial paralysis, eyelid twitch, epistaxis, toothache, swelling of lips and cheek.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The branches of the facial and infraorbital nerves.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, directly inferior to the pupil, at the same level as the inferior border of the ala of the nose. Note: When looking straight ahead, ST3 is located at the intersection of the vertical line of the pupil and the horizontal line of the inferior border of the ala of the nose.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6221269"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Juliao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001771"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006906"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>S 3</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Stomach 3</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the facial and infraorbital arteries and veins.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>ST 3</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5888779 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5888779">
