        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 163. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>淸(清)冷(令)淵(渊)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior brachial cutaneous nerve and the muscular branch of the radial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterior aspect of the arm, on the line connecting the prominence of olecranon with the acromial angle, 2 B-cun proximal to the prominence of the olecranon. Note: With the elbow extended, 2 B-cun superior to the prominence of the olecranon.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3898257"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Qinglengyuan</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001461"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006810"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001460"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>SJ 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>San Jiao 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>TB 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>TH 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>TW 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Triple Burner 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Triple Energizer 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Triple Heater 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Triple Warmer 11</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The terminal branches of the median collateral artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>TE 11</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


