        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 34. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>商陽(阳)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2954517"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Toothache, sore throat, swelling of the submandibular region, numbness of fingers, febrile diseases with anhidrosis, loss of consciousness.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The palmar digital proprial nerve derived from the median nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the index finger, radial to the distal phalanx, 0.1 f-cun proximal-lateral to the radial corner of the index fingernail, at the intersection of the vertical line of the radial border of the fingernail and the horizontal line of the base of the index fingernail.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4610474"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture 0.1 inch, or prick the point to cause bleeding.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shangyang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004300"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011274"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003622"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Large Intestine 1</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The arterial and venous network formed by the dorsal digital arteries and veins.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LI 1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


