        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 46. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>四白</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Redness, pain and itching of the eye, facial paralysis, twitching of eye lids, pain in the face.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The branches of the facial nerve. The point is right on the course of the infraorbital nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, in the infraorbital foramen.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6221269"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.2-0.3 inch. It is not advisable to puncture deeply.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Sibai</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0018407"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>S 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Stomach 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of facial artery and vein, the infraorbital artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>ST 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


