        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 189. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>陽(阳)交</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5595374"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Fullness of the chest and hypochondriac region, muscular atrophy and paralysis of the leg.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The lateral sural cutaneous nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the fibular aspect of the leg, posterior to the fibula, 7 B-cun proximal to the prominence of the lateral malleolus. Note: GB35 is located 1 B-cun distal to the midpoint of the line connecting the prominence of the lateral malleolus and the lateral end of the popliteal crease, posterior to gB36.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5283975"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.8 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Yangjiao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001446"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012291"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795330"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003823"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>G 35</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Gallbladder 35</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the peroneal artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GB 35</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6728804 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6728804">
