        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 115. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>次髎(髎)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Low back pain, hernia, irregular menstruation, leukorrhea, dysmenorrhea, nocturnal emission, impotence, enuresis, dysuria, muscular atrophy, pain, numbness and motor impairment of the lower extremities.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The posterior ramus of the second sacral nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the sacral region, in the second posterior sacral foramen. Note: The second posterior sacral foramen is located in the depression, midway be- tween the posterior superior iliac spine and the spinous process of the second sacral vertebra.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Chiliao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004623"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0013710"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795314"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005473"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 32</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 32</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 32</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 32</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The posterior branches of the lateral sacral artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 32</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


