        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 216. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>素髎(髎)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Loss of consciousness, nasal obstruction, epistaxis, rhinorrhea, rosacea.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The external nasal branch of the anterior ethmoidal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, at the tip of the nose.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.2-0.3 inch, or prick to cause bleeding.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Suliao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000004"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0012128"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 25</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The lateral nasal branches of the facial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 25</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6927551 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6927551">
