        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 116. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>中髎(髎)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Low back pain, constipation, diarrhea, dysuria, irregular menstruation, morbid leukorrhea.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>On the course of the posterior ramus of the third sacral nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the sacral region, in the third posterior sacral foramen. Note: The third posterior sacral foramen is located in the first depression, moving downward from BL32.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Zhongliao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795315"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005473"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 33</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 33</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 33</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 33</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The posterior branches of the lateral sacral artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 33</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6929444 -->

