        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 127. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>承筋</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Spasm of the gastrocnemius, hemorrhoids, acute lower back pam.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The medial sural cutaneous nerve; deeper, the tibial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the posterior aspect of the leg, between the two muscle bellies of the gastrocne- mius muscle, 5 B-cun distal to the popliteal crease. Note: Midway between BL55 and BL57.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Chengjin</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001388"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795330"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003823"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 56</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 56</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 56</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 56</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The small saphenous vein; deeper, the posterior tibial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 56</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7646636 -->

