        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 215. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>神(神)庭</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Epilepsy, anxiety, palpitation, insomnia, headache, vertigo, rhinorrhea.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The branch of the frontal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the head, 0.5 B-cun superior to the anterior hairline, on the anterior median line. Note: When the anterior hairline is unclear or changed, GV 24 is located 3.5 B-cun superior to the midpoint between the medial ends of the eyebrows.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch, or prick to cause bleeding.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Shenting</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010163"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795292"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000033"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 24</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 24</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branch of the frontal artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 24</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


