        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 43. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>口禾髎(髎)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Nasal obstruction, epistaxis, deviation of the mouth.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The anastomotic branch of the facial nerve and the infraorbital nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, at the same level as the midpoint of the philtrum, inferior to the lateral margin of the nostril. Note: 0.5 B-cun laterals to GV 26. Remarks: Alternative location for LI19 - On the face, at the same level as the junc- tion of the upper one third and lower two thirds of the philtrum, inferior to the lateral margin of the nostril.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4610474"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely 0.2-0.3 inch.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Kouheliao</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005402"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005928"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Large Intestine 19</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The superior labial branches of the facial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LI 19</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


