        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 34. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>二間(间)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_9857829"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Blurring of vision, Epistaxis, toothache, sore throat, febrile diseases.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The dorsal digital nerve of the radial nerve, and the palmar digital proper nerve of the median nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the index finger, in the depression distal to the radial side of the second metacarpophalangeal joint, at the border between the red and white flesh.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4610474"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.2-0.3 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Erjian</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003695"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003622"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Large Intestine 2</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The dorsal digital and plamar digital proper arteries and veins derived from the radial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>LI 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


