        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 126. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>胞(胞)肓</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Borborygmus, abdominal distension, pain in the lower back, anuria.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The superior cluneal nerves; deeper, the superior gluteal nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the buttock region, at the same level as the second posterior sacral foramen, 3 B-cun lateral to the median sacral crest. Note: BL53, BL28 and BL32 are located at the same level as the second posterior sacral foramen.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Baohuang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0741680"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795314"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0013691"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 53</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 53</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 53</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 53</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The superior gluteal artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 53</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


