        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 231. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>承漿(浆)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Facial puffiness, swel1ing of the gums, toothache, salivation, mental disorders, deviation of the eyes and mouth.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The branch of the facial nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>On the face, in the depression in the centre of the mentolabial sulcus.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6789717"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely upward 0.2-0.3 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Chengjiang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795327"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001456"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Conception Vessel 24</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>RN 24</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Ren 24</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The branches of the inferior labial artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>CV 24</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


