        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 208. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>至陽(阳)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Jaundice, cough, asthma, stiffness of the back, pain in the chest and back.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The medial branch of the posterior ramus of the seventh thoracic nerve.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the upper back region, in the depression inferior to the spinous process of the seventh thoracic vertebra (T7), on the posterior median line. Note: The depression inferior to the spinous process of the seventh thoracic vertebra (T7) which is at the intersection of two imaginary lines: the posterior midline and the horizontal line of the inferior border of the inferior angle of the scapula.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_0386099"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely upward 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Zhiyang</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004632"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006849"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795312"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008231"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Du 9</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Governor Vessel 9</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The posterior branch of the seventh intercostal artery.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>GV 9</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


