        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Ch. 10, Sec. III, The Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Headache, eye diseases, deviation of the eyes and mouth.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the depression about one finger breadth posterior to the midpoint between the lateral end of the eyebrow and the outer canthus.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch, or prick to cause bleeding.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
