        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 108. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <TARA:hasChineseLabel>肝兪(俞)</TARA:hasChineseLabel>
        <TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6904005"/>
        <TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>Jaundice, pain in the hypochondriac region, redness of the eye, blurring of vision, night blindness, mental disorders, epilepsy, backache, spitting of blood, epistaxis.</TARA:hasIndicationsDescription>
        <TARA:hasInnervationDescription>The medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the ninth and tenth thoracic nerves; deeper, their lateral branches.</TARA:hasInnervationDescription>
        <TARA:hasLocationalDescription>In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the ninth thoracic vertebra (T9), 1.5 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line.</TARA:hasLocationalDescription>
        <TARA:hasMeridian rdf:resource="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476"/>
        <TARA:hasMethodDescription>Puncture obliquely 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</TARA:hasMethodDescription>
        <TARA:hasPinyinLabel>Ganshu</TARA:hasPinyinLabel>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004633"/>
        <TARA:hasRelatedLocation rdf:resource="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795312"/>
        <TARA:hasSurfaceLocation rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0008231"/>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>B 18</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Back-Shu Point of the Liver</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Bladder 18</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>UB 18</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasSynonym>Urinary Bladder 18</TARA:hasSynonym>
        <TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>The medial branches of the posterior branches of the intercostal artery and vein.</TARA:hasVasculatureDescription>
        <rdfs:label>BL 18</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


