    <!-- http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/unclassified_imported_term -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/unclassified_imported_term">
        <rdfs:comment>This class serves as a generic &quot;placeholder&quot; superclass for all unclassified imported terms referenced by some of the asserted axioms in the TARA Acupoints ontology and its knowledge base. Its subclasses are terms imported from the UBERON, MONDO, and HPO ontologies.

Note 1: Each subclass reuses the exact IRI and label from its source ontology, without any additional logical axioms from the source ontology. This design choice avoids importing the full UBERON, MONDO, and HP ontologies while still preserving the labels required by the referencing axioms, and it eliminates the reasoning overhead those imports would impose on the core TARA ontology classes.

Note 2: The full classification and axioms for the terms under this class can be obtained at query time by loading the external ontologies (UBERON, MONDO, HPO) alongside the TARA Acupoints ontology into a high-performance graph database such as Stardog or GraphDB.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>unclassified imported term</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


